From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:30:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] Document 0.3.0: user manual, architecture, tutorial and
 README

Add docs/user-manual.md: installation, concepts, the complete model,
candidate, budget and result reference from the code, statuses and
error messages, the Python, Rust and CLI APIs, a scenario cookbook,
optimization with penalties, campaigns, reproducibility, performance
tips and troubleshooting. Its 17 Python blocks run against the
installed wheel and their outputs, like the shell outputs, are copied
from actual runs; release_checks.py now executes them after the
tutorial's blocks.

Review docs/architecture.md against the 0.3.0 code: the matrix API,
grouping and lane kernels, the persistent pool, typed metrics and
decoding, and a Performance section with the 0.2.0-to-0.3.0 table, the
phase breakdown, per-call costs from Python, worker scaling, installed
Python optimization timings and API guidance, all citing evidence.
Update README.md and docs/tutorial.md for the matrix API and benchmark
flags, use American spelling in the model card, and add
validation/python_call_costs.py with its 0.2.0 and 0.3.0 evidence and
the installed optimization runs.

